Z||000000||88CoupeV6||06-04-2001||11:35 AM||||here is Why<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1249362&a=13158498&p=49795347&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P>I will post more details about the show latter. I have to go help someone work on there Chevy.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh <B>(known by TheFiero64 for first 1239 posts)</B><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">    <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
Z||000001||Fiero5||06-04-2001||12:48 PM||||Wow! What a nice day we ended up having for the show. Even with the very strong <BR>possibility of bad weather, we had a good enough turn out of Fieros to win the club participation award!! Fred "Mr. Potatohead" Clark accepted the award on behalf of the club due to a missing NEFA club President right at that time. Scoopy Doo, &gt;achem&lt;, Ray Paulk where are you?<P>Anyway,<BR>The Trans-Am Firebird class had a pretty strong showing, as did the GTO class even with the weather putting a cloud over the show and causing a much smaller attendance than usual. But it was the Fiero class that was the talk of the show this year.<P>Those that were present:<P>Fred Clark in a maroon 87 coupe<BR>Dave Paulk with Dad in his "in process" T-Top fastback conversion (88 Formula?)<BR>Les Sandy in his red T-Top 2M4 (86?)<BR>Matt Turner in his white 86SE<BR>Josh Bumpus (and Jaime) in his red 88 coupe<BR>Rob and Renee' Dabrowski in Rob's black 86 GT<BR>Phil & Gwen Randolph in Phils now very famous yellow 88 Formula<BR>Marian Kelley with her newly unveiled "in process" black 88 Formula fastback<BR>Myself with my red 86 SS<BR>Jody Lemos in his red 86 GT<P>If I missed someone, made a mistake in the car year/description or screwed up the spelling of your name I apologize.<P>We had not one, but two ties for trophies within our Fiero class "Q". I will wait for 88coupeV6 (Josh) to announce the winners as I don't want to mess up the order of who tied for second with him and so on.<P>MikeB. stopped by and visited. He has sold/traded with a few club members with some Fiero stuff including some sweet Fieros in the past. This includes the recent awesome 88 that Marian (Fiero2) now owns. Marian<BR>was finally able to meet him and show him what she has done to date with the car. He was amazed at wheat we had done on it in about a months time. What a transformation!<BR>Yes, I will finally be able to post some pics of her new show car.<P>Eric Schneck sadly did not have a running Fiero to bring, but still made<BR>the trip with Beth to join his fellow Fiero brothers and sisters for a<BR>great day.<P>After the show wrapped up at around 4pm, a few of us made the cruise to Coventry RI behind the award winning/latest Hot Rod issue yellow Formula to Phil & Gwen's home for great food and great conversation. A bonus was the awesome desserts that Gwen had picked up for us to get really stuffed on after dinner.<P>I took quite a few pictures at the show, including a shot of each Fiero individually. I think Rob D. took a bunch also. I should have mine ready for posting on a Pennocks thread or two by tomorrow.<P>Thanks to all who braved the drive (for some it was a good 3 plus hour drive) and possible bad weather, as it turned out to be a great day. What else would anyone expect when a group of "rowdy" Fiero owners get together? We really showed the other Pontiac people what these Fiero's and their owners are all about. <P>Steve<P>------------------<BR>                         [IMG][i00mg]http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero9-86SS1.jpg[/img][/IMG]                       <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||6
Z||000002||Fiero5||06-04-2001||12:51 PM||||Oooops.<P>------------------<BR>                        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero9-86SS1.jpg">                        <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||12
Z||000003||88CoupeV6||06-04-2001||03:20 PM||||Well, I think Fiero5 did a great job of describing the day. P.S. Steve Can I use that for the next Newsletter?? I had a great time and was glad the weather turned around for us. I loved seeing all the old cars and the 10 Fieros. I can't wait for the show in NH next weekend.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The winners were<P>3rd<BR>Les Sandy in his red T-Top (87 I think)<BR>Rob and Renee' Dabrowski in Rob's black 86 GT<P>2nd<BR>Matt Turner in his white 86SE<BR>Me Josh Bumpus (and Jaime) in my 88coupeV6<P>1st<BR>Phil & Gwen Randolph in Phils famous yellow 88 Formula<P><P>------------------<BR>Josh <B>(known by TheFiero64 for first 1239 posts)</B><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">    <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
